E.4 Anticipated Challenges and Mitigation

Challenge: Bureaucratic inertia and slow administrative processes in Moroccan public universities may deter diaspora researchers accustomed to agile environments.
Mitigation: Grant RFUA pilot institutions special administrative autonomy, including fast-track hiring, procurement, and grant management processes.

Challenge: Saturation of repatriated researchers in Casablanca-Rabat axis, neglecting other regions.
Mitigation: Offer additional incentives (housing allowances, regional development bonuses) for placements in Fez, Marrakech, Agadir, or Tangier-based RFUA nodes.

Challenge: Insufficient critical mass in a specific subfield, leaving a repatriated researcher isolated.
Mitigation: Prioritize cluster hiring in targeted domains (e.g., recruit a team of three AI researchers simultaneously) rather than piecemeal appointments.


